  <graph edgedefault="directed">
    <node id="0">
      <data key="d5">CloudFormation</data>
      <data key="d6">CloudFormation</data>
      <data key="d7">The internal cloud team, AWS and Evertz scrubbed and edited about 40 YAML templates to make the deployment repeatable and expandable.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="1">
      <data key="d5">S3</data>
      <data key="d6">S3</data>
      <data key="d7">Stores the master files for all brands. Files arrive from Atlanta through Aspera and are registered in Evertz Mediator.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="2">
      <data key="d5">ASG</data>
      <data key="d6">AutoScaling</data>
      <data key="d7">Auto Scaling groups support the primary and backup EC2 instances for each channel.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="3">
      <data key="d5">EC2 Top</data>
      <data key="d6">EC2</data>
      <data key="d7">One AZ in us-east-1 runs Evertz ORT/Playtime for 10 channels (primary and backup). Redundant with the other AZs.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="4">
      <data key="d5">EC2 Middle</data>
      <data key="d6">EC2</data>
      <data key="d7">One AZ in us-east-1 runs Evertz ORT/Playtime for 10 channels (primary and backup). Redundant with the other AZs.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="5">
      <data key="d5">EC2 Bottom</data>
      <data key="d6">EC2</data>
      <data key="d7">One AZ in us-east-1 runs Evertz ORT/Playtime for 10 channels (primary and backup). Redundant with the other AZs.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="6">
      <data key="d5">Direct Connect</data>
      <data key="d6">DirectConnect</data>
      <data key="d7">Carries the playout back on-premises as a unicast signal over Evertz CloudBridge, which is installed at each end of the connection.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="7">
      <data key="d5">NYC Satellite</data>
      <data key="d6">ThirdParty</data>
      <data key="d7">Hudson Yards BCP uplink for 8 channels. Runs CloudBridge in New York.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="8">
      <data key="d5">ATL Satellite</data>
      <data key="d6">ThirdParty</data>
      <data key="d7">Atlanta uplink that distributes channels to affiliates.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="9">
      <data key="d5">TWD/CNN Center</data>
      <data key="d6">ThirdParty</data>
      <data key="d7">Techwood/CNN Center site. Linear Ops quality-checks master files here. An auto changeover switch chooses between Techwood, CNN Center and cloud playout. The signal is compressed here before uplink. Runs CloudBridge in Atlanta.</data>
    </node>
    <edge source="0" target="3" id="0">
      <data key="d8">2</data>
      <data key="d9">Deploys the system from about 40 YAML templates in a repeatable process.</data>
      <data key="d10">0</data>
      <data key="d11">control</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1" target="3" id="0">
      <data key="d8">0</data>
      <data key="d9">Once registered in Evertz Mediator, the files are transferred to the local EC2 instance running Evertz ORT.</data>
      <data key="d10">1</data>
      <data key="d11">data</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1" target="4" id="0">
      <data key="d8">0</data>
      <data key="d9">Once registered in Evertz Mediator, the files are transferred to the local EC2 instance running Evertz ORT.</data>
      <data key="d10">1'</data>
      <data key="d11">data</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1" target="5" id="0">
      <data key="d8">0</data>
      <data key="d9">Once registered in Evertz Mediator, the files are transferred to the local EC2 instance running Evertz ORT.</data>
      <data key="d10">1''</data>
      <data key="d11">data</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2" target="3" id="0">
      <data key="d8">3</data>
      <data key="d9">The Auto Scaling group supports the primary and backup instances.</data>
      <data key="d10">0</data>
      <data key="d11">control</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2" target="4" id="0">
      <data key="d8">3</data>
      <data key="d9">The Auto Scaling group supports the primary and backup instances.</data>
      <data key="d10">0'</data>
      <data key="d11">control</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2" target="5" id="0">
      <data key="d8">3</data>
      <data key="d9">The Auto Scaling group supports the primary and backup instances.</data>
      <data key="d10">0''</data>
      <data key="d11">control</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="3" target="6" id="0">
      <data key="d8">0</data>
      <data key="d9">Evertz Playtime playout is sent as a unicast signal over CloudBridge.</data>
      <data key="d10">2</data>
      <data key="d11">data</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4" target="6" id="0">
      <data key="d8">0</data>
      <data key="d9">Evertz Playtime playout is sent as a unicast signal over CloudBridge.</data>
      <data key="d10">2'</data>
      <data key="d11">data</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5" target="6" id="0">
      <data key="d8">0</data>
      <data key="d9">Evertz Playtime playout is sent as a unicast signal over CloudBridge.</data>
      <data key="d10">2''</data>
      <data key="d11">data</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6" target="9" id="0">
      <data key="d8">0</data>
      <data key="d9">The 'X chain', a tertiary path to air back on-premises, feeding the auto changeover switch.</data>
      <data key="d10">3</data>
      <data key="d11">data</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6" target="7" id="0">
      <data key="d8">1</data>
      <data key="d9">BCP path over Direct Connect to Hudson Yards for 8 channels, then fed to the uplink.</data>
      <data key="d10">0</data>
      <data key="d11">data</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9" target="1" id="0">
      <data key="d8">0</data>
      <data key="d9">Master files that Linear Ops quality-checked in Atlanta are sent to S3 with Aspera.</data>
      <data key="d10">0</data>
      <data key="d11">data</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9" target="8" id="0">
      <data key="d8">0</data>
      <data key="d9">The signal is compressed and sent to the uplink for distribution to affiliates.</data>
      <data key="d10">4</data>
      <data key="d11">data</data>
    </edge>
    <data key="d0">WarnerMedia HBO Cloud Linear Playout</data>
    <data key="d1">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hMK2NJ-q9nc</data>
    <data key="d2">This cloud linear playout runs 30 channels in AWS us-east-1, with 10 channels per AZ and a primary and backup for each channel. It started as a business continuity (BCP) solution. It uses Evertz Mediator, ORT and Playtime software on EC2. Evertz CloudBridge runs at each end of the connection: in AWS, New York and Atlanta. The goal is five-nines availability. The deployment is repeatable through about 40 CloudFormation YAML templates. Future plans include live venue switching on the ORT and in-cloud multiplexing or compression handed directly to MVPDs.</data>
    <data key="d3">Media &amp; Entertainment, Broadcast Playout, Hybrid Cloud, Business Continuity</data>
    <data key="d4">True</data>
  </graph>
